Package: bulkdeconv
Type: Package
Title: Cell-Type Deconvolution of Tumor Bulk RNA-Seq Through One Function
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Daiki", "Kumakura", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "55353329+DaikiKumakura@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Runs published cell-type deconvolution and cell-abundance methods
    for bulk RNA-seq of tumor tissue (human or mouse) through a single
    function, bulkdeconv(data, expr, species, method). Each method runs in a
    separate R process from its own isolated library at a pinned version, so
    methods with conflicting dependencies can coexist. Input is checked
    before anything runs, a registry records what each method needs and how
    its output can be compared, and results come back in one standard layout
    with metadata and quality information. Only methods that need no
    registration are included. Fifteen methods are implemented in the package
    itself.
